The Gradle build files under mod/ (build.gradle.kts, settings.gradle.kts,
gradle.properties, dependencies.gradle, repositories.gradle, gtnhShared/, the
Gradle wrapper) come from the GT New Horizons mod template
(https://github.com/GTNewHorizons/ExampleMod1.7.10), which is under the MIT
License, Copyright (c) 2021 Johann Bernhardt.

The brain-side production planner directly reuses the original calculation
implementation from GTNH Factory Flow:
  https://github.com/jackwrichards/gtnh-factory-flow
  Copyright (c) 2026 Samiracle64
  Copyright (c) 2026 jackwrichards
  MIT License

Its corresponding original mod, GTNH Planner, supplies the machine catalogue
and independent machine-calculation reference data and informs this integration:
  https://github.com/jackwrichards/gtnh-planner-mod
  Copyright (c) 2026 Sbancuz
  MIT License

This integration uses those original projects, not a translated release. The
upstream calculators, schemas, data and declarations are not claimed as original
Alu AI Player code. Pinned sources, copied-file hashes, local changes, build
instructions and runtime hashes are recorded in:
  brain/vendor/gtnh-planner/provenance.json
  brain/vendor/gtnh-planner/source-files.json
  brain/vendor/gtnh-planner/mod-files.json

The calculator distribution includes HiGHS/highs-js and bundled Zod. Esbuild is
used to generate the local bundles. Their MIT copyright and license notices are
preserved, together with the upstream project notices, in:
  brain/vendor/gtnh-planner/licenses/
  brain/vendor/gtnh-planner/upstream/LICENSE
  brain/vendor/gtnh-planner/mod/LICENSE

This repository does not distribute GTNH mod jars, client/server packs or game
textures. The local item table, recipe book, quest book, guide pages, icons and
textures read by the brain (brain/packdata/) are generated on your own machine
from your own copy of the client pack and are not part of this repository; they
stay under the licenses of their authors. The planner's small upstream machine
catalogues and calculation test fixtures are included under the source projects'
MIT terms; they are not an export of any user's server, inventory or conversations.
